AB  - Delayed gastric emptying occurs with glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist (GLP-1RA) use but small intestinal or colonic transit delays in isolation or combined with gastric delays are less established.1 Factors associated with GLP-1RA delays are incompletely defined, and their reversibility with GLP-1RA cessation is uncertain. Tachyphyaxis of emptying delays to prolonged use is observed in small studies but is unconfirmed in large cohorts.2.
